Noto Sans Regular and Bold, used by the PDF export (src/lib/exportPdf.ts).

Source: https://github.com/notofonts/notofonts.github.io/tree/main/fonts/NotoSans/unhinted/ttf
Project: https://github.com/notofonts/latin-greek-cyrillic
License: SIL Open Font License 1.1, in OFL.txt next to this file.

These are subsets, so the PDF stays small. They keep Latin (including
Vietnamese), Greek, Cyrillic, and common punctuation, and drop hinting and
OpenType layout tables, which jsPDF doesn't use. Made with fontTools:

  pyftsubset NotoSans-Regular.ttf --output-file=public/fonts/NotoSans-Regular.ttf \
    --unicodes="U+0020-007E,U+00A0-036F,U+0370-03FF,U+0400-052F,U+1E00-1EFF,U+2000-206F,U+20A0-20CF,U+2100-214F,U+2190-21FF,U+2212" \
    --layout-features='' --no-hinting --drop-tables+=DSIG,GDEF,GPOS,GSUB --notdef-outline

Run the same command on NotoSans-Bold.ttf.

Chinese, Japanese, Korean, and other scripts aren't covered. The PDF leaves
those characters out.
